{"seq":12,"slug":"design-patterns","title":"设计模式","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":7,"docCount":26,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns","rating":{"composite":4.02,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.4,"coverage":4,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.42,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"设计模式-简介\">设计模式 简介</h1><p>设计模式是软件工程中经过反复验证的、针对特定设计问题的通用解决方案。它们不是可以直接复制粘贴的代码，而是一套描述如何在不同场景下组织代码结构的模板和思维框架。掌握设计模式，意味着你能够用经过实战检验的方式来构建灵活、可维护、可扩展的软件系统。</p>\n<p>本手册面向希望系统性学习设计模式的开发者。无论你是正在夯实面向对象基础的初学者，还是希望在架构设计中做出更优决策的中高级工程师，都能从中获益。所有代码示例均使用 TypeScript 编写，结合类型系统的优势让模式的结构更加清晰直观。</p>\n<p>第一章<strong>基础概念</strong>从设计模式的起源与定义出发，带你理解模式的本质——它是对常见问题的命名与抽象。我们还将系统梳理面向对象编程的核心原则（SOLID），并讨论如何在实际项目中选择合适的模式。</p>\n<p>第二章<strong>创建型模式</strong>聚焦于对象的创建机制。单例、工厂方法与抽象工厂、建造者、原型——这些模式帮助你将对象的创建逻辑与使用逻辑解耦，让系统在扩展新类型时无需修改已有代码。</p>\n<p>第三章<strong>结构型模式</strong>关注类和对象的组合方式。适配器、装饰器、代理、外观、组合——它们提供了在不修改现有代码的前提下扩展功能和简化接口的优雅手段。</p>\n<p>第四章<strong>行为型模式</strong>处理对象之间的职责分配和通信机制。观察者、策略、命令、状态、迭代器与职责链——这些模式让你能够灵活地管理算法选择、事件通知、请求处理等复杂交互。</p>\n<p>第五章<strong>架构模式</strong>将视角提升到系统层面。MVC/MVP/MVVM 的演进、整洁架构的分层原则、依赖注入的实现策略——帮助你在更大的尺度上组织代码。</p>\n<p>第六章<strong>函数式模式</strong>引入函数式编程的视角。高阶函数与闭包、不可变性与纯函数、Monad 与 Functor——这些概念在现代 TypeScript 开发中日益重要，与传统 OOP 模式形成互补。</p>\n<p>第七章<strong>实践篇</strong>将所有知识融会贯通。从如何通过重构引入模式，到识别和避免反模式，再到在 TypeScript 项目中落地模式的最佳实践——确保你不只是&quot;知道&quot;模式，而是能够&quot;用好&quot;模式。</p>\n<p>设计模式不是银弹，过度使用反而会增加复杂性。本手册的目标是帮助你建立模式直觉——知道何时该用、何时不该用、以及如何根据具体场景做出权衡。让我们开始这段从理论到实践的学习旅程。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础概念","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-are-design-patterns","title":"什么是设计模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/foundations/what-are-design-patterns"},{"seq":2,"slug":"oop-principles-solid","title":"面向对象原则与 SOLID","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/foundations/oop-principles-solid"},{"seq":3,"slug":"choosing-patterns","title":"如何选择设计模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/foundations/choosing-patterns"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"creational","title":"创建型模式","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/creational","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"singleton","title":"单例模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/creational/singleton"},{"seq":2,"slug":"factory-method-and-abstract-factory","title":"工厂方法与抽象工厂","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/creational/factory-method-and-abstract-factory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"builder","title":"建造者模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/creational/builder"},{"seq":4,"slug":"prototype","title":"原型模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/creational/prototype"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"structural","title":"结构型模式","docCount":5,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"adapter","title":"适配器模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural/adapter"},{"seq":2,"slug":"decorator","title":"装饰器模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural/decorator"},{"seq":3,"slug":"proxy","title":"代理模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural/proxy"},{"seq":4,"slug":"facade","title":"外观模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural/facade"},{"seq":5,"slug":"composite","title":"组合模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/structural/composite"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"behavioral","title":"行为型模式","docCount":5,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"observer","title":"观察者模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral/observer"},{"seq":2,"slug":"strategy","title":"策略模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral/strategy"},{"seq":3,"slug":"command","title":"命令模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral/command"},{"seq":4,"slug":"state","title":"状态模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral/state"},{"seq":5,"slug":"iterator-and-chain-of-responsibility","title":"迭代器与职责链模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/behavioral/iterator-and-chain-of-responsibility"}]},{"seq":5,"slug":"architectural","title":"架构模式","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/architectural","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mvc-mvp-mvvm","title":"MVC / MVP / MVVM 架构模式对比","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/architectural/mvc-mvp-mvvm"},{"seq":2,"slug":"clean-architecture","title":"整洁架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/architectural/clean-architecture"},{"seq":3,"slug":"dependency-injection","title":"依赖注入","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/architectural/dependency-injection"}]},{"seq":6,"slug":"functional-patterns","title":"函数式模式","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/functional-patterns","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"higher-order-functions-and-closures","title":"高阶函数与闭包","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/functional-patterns/higher-order-functions-and-closures"},{"seq":2,"slug":"immutability-and-pure-functions","title":"不可变性与纯函数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/functional-patterns/immutability-and-pure-functions"},{"seq":3,"slug":"monads-and-functors","title":"Monad 与 Functor","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/functional-patterns/monads-and-functors"}]},{"seq":7,"slug":"practice","title":"实践篇","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"refactoring-to-patterns","title":"重构到模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/practice/refactoring-to-patterns"},{"seq":2,"slug":"anti-patterns","title":"反模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/practice/anti-patterns"},{"seq":3,"slug":"patterns-in-typescript","title":"TypeScript 中的模式实践","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/design-patterns/practice/patterns-in-typescript"}]}]}